{
  "message": "For everyday purchases, the strongest options I found are:",
  "options": [
    {
      "card": "Platinum Rewards Card",
      "cash_back": "10.0% on all eligible purchases",
      "annual_fee": "$200",
      "best_for": "Maximizing rewards if your spending is high enough to offset the annual fee",
      "notes": "Rewards can be redeemed after reaching $15. A separate benefit guide says you may earn a $150 annual-fee rebate by spending $7,500 per month."
    },
    {
      "card": "Gold Rewards Card",
      "cash_back": "2.5% on all purchases",
      "annual_fee": "$0",
      "requirement": "Active Rho-Bank+ premium subscription required",
      "best_for": "A strong flat-rate cash-back option if you already have, or want, the subscription",
      "other_terms": "17.99% APR on carried balances and 0% foreign transaction fee"
    },
    {
      "card": "Crypto-Cash Back Card",
      "cash_back": "2.0% on eligible spending",
      "annual_fee": "$75",
      "best_for": "Someone comfortable redeeming rewards into cryptocurrency",
      "notes": "Crypto redemption requires at least $30 and has a 1.25% conversion fee. The card has a 19.49% APR on carried balances."
    },
    {
      "card": "Silver Rewards Card",
      "cash_back": "1.0% outside its top bonus categories",
      "annual_fee": "$0",
      "best_for": "A no-fee option, especially if your spending matches its bonus categories",
      "other_terms": "0% introductory APR for the first year, then 18.99%; foreign transaction fee is 2.75% without a premium subscription."
    }
  ],
  "recommendation": "If you want straightforward cash back without paying an annual card fee, the Gold Rewards Card appears strongest, provided the required Rho-Bank+ subscription is worthwhile. If you want the highest advertised rate and spend substantially, consider Platinum. If you prefer conventional statement-credit or checking-account cash back rather than crypto, Gold or Platinum are better fits.",
  "important_note": "I found complete details for Silver, Gold, Platinum, and Crypto-Cash Back, but not enough current personal-card terms to accurately compare the Bronze Rewards Card beyond its $0 annual fee. I also recommend paying the balance in full, since carrying a balance can outweigh the rewards through interest."
}
